  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14218283/assets/62474d31ab2981d6173671acb875ec401a51c230994e60e10421d385f2e099a9.png)\n\nConsider the solid curve $y=f(x)$ and the dashed curve $y=f(x)+b$ shown above. What is the value of $b?$",
  "worked_solution": "The graph of $y=f(x)+b$ can be obtained from the graph of $y=f(x)$ by translating it $6$ units *down*. So, $b=-6.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14218283/assets/3fcbd6ce5ea6543fea0038df30e8f31db18c82ceefa975aaaec1854d85766eab.png)",
